# Panel 260's R2 (provisional, author ratification pending): what lies under
# the runtime's `vendor/` is the C a member compiles inside itself, never a
# file of the platform layer. A header of the program's own including the
# vendored Monocypher header for a type's size binds nothing of the layer: its
# group says nothing and the program builds and links none of the layer (the
# critic's `vendorinc`, refused at `build` by the route built first).
extern "sizes.h"
    function sizes_answer() -> i64

function main()
    print(sizes_answer() > 0)
